  "body": "**Hold for the quality-binding correction in PR #2999 for #2984 before machine use or merge.** A preexisting controller quality with the same generic name can select a different target, pass count and wire offset. The original tests establish the plotted geometry on the tested control. They do not establish the requested quality on another installation.\n\nStacked on #2948. The parent is a fork branch. This draft targets upstream main. Review the [native writer changes above the machine template](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/08601a2bc50abcbe2e550c86d3f9e708cbd49071...83affaca1bf4920ed07e29bf7c52bf9c48561b80).\n\n## Change\n\nThe desktop Post command and cam.post write a native Agie job directory with linked ISO, SBR and SBL files. CamCraft writes the nominal contour in Rust and selects resident control technology. The post validates the work before it creates the destination. It publishes all three files together and preserves an existing directory.\n\nThe supported case is one vertical rectangular punch in 20 mm stock. Select the Classic 2S template from #2948. Enter the AGIE_QN2 condition for Berco Cut 0.25 mm wire and cold die steel. Select the 1.0 mm separation cut explicitly. The template starts without an installed condition. A cut needs 0.4 mm clearance at each stock face and 3 mm of straight face on each side of the entry. Other contours, tapers, skims, custom X/Y travel limits and additional workpieces are refused.\n\n## Reference material for review\n\nThe contributor's team wrote [Agie-CAM at 11b1bb9](https://github.com/qsmits/Agie-CAM/tree/11b1bb9ef2c752b94b6fefc1f0814acd2e030c42) and released it under the MIT license. This draft retains the license and copyright notice. The implementation reference documents observed controller examples for parts of the JEScript sequence and the resident technology selection. The published guides linked on #2945 give the file roles and some interface arguments. They do not document the full sequence and all defaults. Please review that source against the project rules before merge.\n\nThe controller supplies its own runtime and technology table. This PR includes the writer and original synthetic examples and expected output. It includes no controller image, vendor post, runtime library or technology database.\n\n## Control verification\n\nThe offline Classic Cut 2S control imported a CamCraft-generated 40 by 20 mm punch. Its formal check reported zero errors. It reported warnings for setup, reference values and selected option 131072. Its graphical check plotted the rough pass and three trims outside the nominal punch. Their straight-face offsets were 0.245, 0.155, 0.140 and 0.134 mm. The first passes skipped a 1 mm segment. A later sequence cut that segment and returned to the threading hole at X-30 Y0. The simulated stock extended from Z0 to Z-20. No physical machine cut was made.\n\nThe synthetic example runs from the repository root:\n```sh\ncargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/punch.camscript\n```\nUse a new PUNCH40 destination.\n\n## Final head checks\n\nAt head 83affaca1, all nine native application integration tests passed. The tests include the_native_files_match_the_control_checked_rectangular_punch, qn2_requires_the_rough_wire_size_in_the_mounted_condition and the_work_must_fit_between_each_stated_guide. The ordinary command script generated three files identical byte for byte to the earlier offline control input.\n\nThe unconfigured machine, absent or wrong condition role, missing wire diameter, and missing or unsupported separation each produced a diagnostic and no output directory. Independent verification passed 93 scoped checks: 81 app integration tests, four native writer tests, one geometry test, six existing Post dialog tests and one actual desktop Post button check. Both GUI and CLI output matched all three controller input files byte for byte. Strict all-targets Clippy passed on camcraft-app, camcraft-post, camcraft-geometry and camcraft-ui.\n\nThe quick planner selected a 983-step workspace batch. The heavy planner selected 248 steps. Only the plans ran for those full gates. This PR remains a draft.\n\n## Desktop Post dialog\n\n| Before (Generic ISO) | After (native Agie) |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Generic ISO Post dialog](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/625ef345a047980ab6974df99ea8ca2ac5f783b2/before.png) | ![Native Agie Post dialog](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/625ef345a047980ab6974df99ea8ca2ac5f783b2/after.png) |\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: The Wire EDM desktop and script workflows can post a supported Classic Cut 2S punch as a native Agie job directory.\n\nFixes #2945\n\n",
